{"book":5,"chapter":34,"context":{"chapter":34,"title":"Moses Dies on Nebo","summary":"From the top of Pisgah God shows Moses the whole promised land. Moses dies in Moab at 120 and God buries him in an unknown grave; after thirty days of mourning Joshua leads Israel.","background":"Mount Nebo, in today's Jordan, overlooks the Jordan Valley opposite Jericho. Because the chapter reports Moses' death and says no one knows his grave 'unto this day' (v. 6), it was written by someone after him; a Jewish tradition in the Talmud credits these last verses to Joshua. Aaron had also been mourned thirty days (Numbers 20:29).","customs":[{"term":"Laying on of hands","verses":"34:9","note":"Moses had laid his hands on Joshua to pass on his authority publicly (Numbers 27:18-23)."}],"watchFor":["The view sweeps from north to south across the land (vv. 1–3).","Moses' strength had not faded (v. 7).","'Whom the Lord knew face to face' (v. 10)."],"connections":["Numbers 27:18-23","Numbers 20:29","Matthew 17:3","Jude 1:9"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיַּעַל","vaiya'al","H5927","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he went up"],["מֹשֶׁה","mosheh","H4872","HNpm","Moses"],["מֵעַרְבֹת","me'arvot","H6160","HR/Npl","from [the] desert plains of"],["מוֹאָב","mo'av","H4124","HNpl","Moab"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["הַר","har","H2022","HNcmsc","[the] mountain of"],["נְבוֹ","nevo","H5015","HNpl","Nebo"],["רֹאשׁ","rosh","H7218","HNcmsc","[the] top of"],["הַפִּסְגָּה","hapisgah","H6449","HTd/Npl","<the> Pisgah"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","[is] on"],["פְּנֵי","penei","H6440","HNcmpc","[the] face of"],["יְרֵחוֹ","yerecho","H3405","HNpl","Jericho"],["וַיַּרְאֵהוּ","vaiyar'ehu","H7200","Hc/Vhw3ms/Sp3ms","and he showed him"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["הָאָרֶץ","ha'aretz","H776","HTd/Ncfsa","the land"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַגִּלְעָד","hagil'ad","H1568","HTd/Npl","<the>